# File Length Limit Rule

## Rule Summary
- Source files must not exceed 500 lines.
- Keep components modular and focused.
- Break large classes into smaller components, helper scripts, or sub-resources.

## Enforcement and Verification

### 1. Python Linter
Run the Python lint script to audit file line counts across the repository:
```bash
python scripts/lint_file_lengths.py
```

### 2. Godot Headless Test Suite
The Godot test suite verifies all GDScript file lengths:
```powershell
cmd.exe /c "C:\Users\josep\Desktop\Games\Godot_v4.6.1-stable_win64.exe --headless -s tests/run_tests.gd"
```

## Legacy Files Baseline
- Existing legacy files that exceed 500 lines are tracked in a baseline dictionary.
- Legacy files cannot grow longer than their baseline line count.
- Refactor legacy files below 500 lines when you update them.

